{"id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:riemannian-covering-local-isometry","title":"lem:riemannian-covering-local-isometry","path":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.md","line":903,"body":"","kind":"lemma","status":"not_started","tex":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.tex#lem:riemannian-covering-local-isometry","uses":["[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:riemannian-covering]]","[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:local-isometry]]","[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:smooth-covering-map]]"],"inspired_by":[],"bindings":[],"is_index":false,"body_html":"","formal":[],"tex_content":{"path":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.tex","label":"lem:riemannian-covering-local-isometry","line":1377,"source":"\\begin{lemma}[A Riemannian Covering Is a Local Isometry]\n\\label{lem:riemannian-covering-local-isometry}\n\n\\uses{def:riemannian-covering, def:local-isometry, def:smooth-covering-map}\n\n\n\n\nEvery Riemannian covering is a local isometry.\n\\end{lemma}\n\n\\begin{proof}\n\n\\uses{def:local-isometry,def:smooth-covering-map}\n\\sketch A smooth covering is a local diffeomorphism, and $\\pi^*g=\\tilde g$ means that each local inverse chart preserves the metric.\n\\end{proof}","html":" <p></p><section class=\"theorem\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Lemma</div></section>[A Riemannian Covering Is a Local Isometry] <span class=\"tex-label\" id=\"tex-label-6c656d3a7269656d616e6e69616e2d636f766572696e672d6c6f63616c2d69736f6d65747279\"></span> <p></p><a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23def%3Ariemannian-covering\">↗ def:riemannian-covering</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23def%3Alocal-isometry\">↗ def:local-isometry</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23def%3Asmooth-covering-map\">↗ def:smooth-covering-map</a> <p></p>Every Riemannian covering is a local isometry.  <p></p><section class=\"theorem proof\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Proof</div><p><a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23def%3Alocal-isometry\">↗ def:local-isometry</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23def%3Asmooth-covering-map\">↗ def:smooth-covering-map</a> \\sketch A smooth covering is a local diffeomorphism, and <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\pi ^*g=\\tilde g$\">$\\pi ^*g=\\tilde g$</span> means that each local inverse chart preserves the metric. </p><span class=\"qed\" aria-label=\"证毕\" style=\"display:block;text-align:right\">□</span></section>","warnings":["部分 TeX 排版细节未完整还原（已保留可读内容）: sketch"]},"previous":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:riemannian-covering","next":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:equidimensional-riemannian-submersion-local-isometry","relations":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:riemannian-covering","title":"def:riemannian-covering","label":"def:riemannian-covering"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:local-isometry","title":"def:local-isometry","label":"def:local-isometry"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:smooth-covering-map","title":"def:smooth-covering-map","label":"def:smooth-covering-map"}],"backlinks":[],"copy_context":{"version":1,"level":0,"node":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:riemannian-covering-local-isometry","title":"lem:riemannian-covering-local-isometry","tex":"\\begin{lemma}[A Riemannian Covering Is a Local Isometry]\n\\label{lem:riemannian-covering-local-isometry}\n\n\\uses{def:riemannian-covering, def:local-isometry, def:smooth-covering-map}\n\n\n\n\nEvery Riemannian covering is a local isometry.\n\\end{lemma}\n\n\\begin{proof}\n\n\\uses{def:local-isometry,def:smooth-covering-map}\n\\sketch A smooth covering is a local diffeomorphism, and $\\pi^*g=\\tilde g$ means that each local inverse chart preserves the metric.\n\\end{proof}","source":"tex/references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.tex","description":"","dependencies":[{"node":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:riemannian-covering","title":"def:riemannian-covering","description":""},{"node":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:local-isometry","title":"def:local-isometry","description":""},{"node":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:smooth-covering-map","title":"def:smooth-covering-map","description":""}],"dependencies_omitted":0,"unresolved_dependencies":[],"unresolved_omitted":0}}